  "notes": [
    "<demo-dir> denotes the temporary synthetic directory used by all three file-based commands.",
    "The manifest validator checks declared hashes and IDs; it does not hash referenced observation bytes or establish temporal independence.",
    "The tangent raster keeps empty cells invalid. Lip-sector occupancy is observed coverage, not a physical seal label.",
    "Historical outward axes retain their supplied sign. Proposal camera-facing orientation is opt-in.",
    "Zero observed normals retain finite RGB/geometry support with zero normal channels; query axes must still be valid nonzero directed unit vectors.",
    "The original tangent-raster utility is not part of the v2 B default; the new reference demonstrates projected ring coordinates only.",
    "v2 checks cover declared target-self collision components and Q_inst products, not the real-data collision/Seal teacher.",
    "29 baseline + 26 retained v2 + 26 v3 normal/sampler + 48 v3 contact-boundary checks passed (129 total).",
    "v2 organized normals and one-per-cell queries are retained as regression fixtures, not v3 defaults. Fixed chart, ideal ring geometry and the v2 quality label validator remain shared.",
    "New references construct and evaluate contact geometry in float64. A 1e-12 m roundoff guard is not a sensor-noise allowance or a guarantee for already quantized float32 XYZ.",
    "Harmonic magnitudes k=1,2,3 are incomplete shape summaries; reference tests include high-order and relative-phase counterexamples.",
    "The Gaussian depth-noise example is a fixed synthetic fixture, not a RealSense/stereo measurement or a general noise-reduction factor.",
    "<v3-demo-dir> is a fresh temporary output directory; the demo files were separately read back after generation to verify shapes, valid counts, unique IDs and prefixes."
  ],
